{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nestjs/nest/pulls/5710","id":522565894,"node_id":"MDExOlB1bGxSZXF1ZXN0NTIyNTY1ODk0","html_url":"https://github.com/nestjs/nest/pull/5710","diff_url":"https://github.com/nestjs/nest/pull/5710.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/nestjs/nest/pull/5710.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nestjs/nest/issues/5710","number":5710,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Feat/microservice deserialize error","user":{"login":"jmcdo29","id":28268680,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4MjY4Njgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28268680?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdo29","html_url":"https://github.com/jmcdo29","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdo29/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdo29/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdo29/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdo29/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdo29/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdo29/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdo29/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdo29/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jmcdo29/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## PR Checklist\r\nPlease check if your PR fulfills the following requirements:\r\n\r\n- [X] The commit message follows our guidelines: https://github.com/nestjs/nest/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md\r\n- [X] Tests for the changes have been added (for bug fixes / features)\r\n- [ ] Docs have been added / updated (for bug fixes / features)\r\n\r\n\r\n## PR Type\r\nWhat kind of change does this PR introduce?\r\n\r\n<!-- Please check the one that applies to this PR using \"x\". -->\r\n```\r\n[ ] Bugfix\r\n[X] Feature\r\n[ ] Code style update (formatting, local variables)\r\n[ ] Refactoring (no functional changes, no api changes)\r\n[ ] Build related changes\r\n[ ] CI related changes\r\n[ ] Other... Please describe:\r\n```\r\n\r\n## What is the current behavior?\r\n<!-- Please describe the current behavior that you are modifying, or link to a relevant issue. -->\r\nCurrently, it isn't possible to use a customized `ClientProxy` class with the `ClientsModule`. This means that all errors coming back into the server are not able to be serialized, except for manually doing so on each call, which is cumbersome and a huge overhead.\r\nIssue Number: Fix #5694 \r\n\r\n\r\n## What is the new behavior?\r\n\r\nThere is a new option that can be passed to `ClientsModule.register/Async()` where a `customClass` can be passed in and used instead of one of the standard Nest classes. This `customClass` should `extends ClientProxy` at the very least, but it should more likely `extends Client<Transport>` instead, to get a better hold on what the class should do. There's also two new methods `serializeError` and `serializeData` that are `protected` so they can be overwritten by child classes. This will allow for a better DX by being able to implement custom serialization logic once.\r\n\r\n## Does this PR introduce a breaking change?\r\n```\r\n[ ] Yes\r\n[X] No\r\n```\r\n\r\n<!-- If this PR contains a breaking change, please describe the impact and migration path for existing applications below. -->\r\n\r\n\r\n## Other information","created_at":"2020-11-17T17:07:05Z","updated_at":"2021-05-28T10:25:38Z","closed_at":"2021-02-01T13:26:45Z","merged_at":"2021-02-01T13:26:45Z","merge_commit_sha":"8180e5905cdac1d65d5dd6916b18b3a95a9d4efd","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":532263510,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw1MzIyNjM1MTA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/nestjs/nest/labels/type:%20enhancement%20:wolf:","name":"type: enhancement :wolf:","color":"84b6eb","default":false,"description":""},{"id":851403452,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4NTE0MDM0NTI=","url":"https://api.gi